# Test: a live edit of routing-table reaches the routing-table plugin
# Initial config: routing-table defines red (100).
# After SIGHUP:   routing-table defines red (100) and blue (171).
# Expected: the plugin installs the reloaded tables at apply and logs the
#           registry it published, with both tables counted.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 21, AC-1: the
#            routing-table plugin's verify/apply pair publishes the reloaded
#            name-to-ID map (installRoutingTables).
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while the registry kept the boot tables until a restart.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the "count=2" line is written only by installRoutingTables,
# which only the apply handler calls on a reload. Without the handler the
# count=2 expectation fails. That a route resolves against
# the candidate tables of the same commit is proven in Go by
# TestStaticVerifyResolvesCandidateTable (static/candidate_tables_test.go).

option=env:var=ze.log.routing.table:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
routing-table {
	table red {
		id 100
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Rewritten config: table blue is added, red is unchanged.
tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
routing-table {
	table red {
		id 100
	}
	table blue {
		id 171
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete:then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=routing-table registry loaded.*count=2
expect=stderr:pattern=routing-table registry loaded.*count=1
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
